<binaryimage arch="x86:LE:64:default:gcc">
<!--
    P3 simplification quiescence, P0 option opaquepredicate (default off):
    the proofs beyond low bits and bitwise identities, and the value
    `globals`. The script loads an in-tree linked image of opaqueglobal.c
    (source beside it): clang -O0, x86-64, freestanding and static.

    Narrow inputs (kuna_opaquedomain.rs): (v * v * v - v) % 3 is zero and
    v * v is not negative for every byte v, so cube and square lose their
    dead arm; cubewide tests a 32-bit v, for which the product wraps, and
    stays.

    Implied (kuna_opaqueimplied.rs): inside `if (v > 5)` the test `v <= 5` is
    false (again), inside `if (v < 5)` so is `v > 10` (range); `v > 2` is
    still open there (rangekeep).

    Identical arms (kuna_opaquearms.rs): same and samecall run the same
    operations whichever way their branch goes, so one copy remains; differ
    multiplies by another constant in one arm and keeps both.

    Never-written globals (kuna_opaqueglobals.rs, value `globals` only): no
    instruction stores to y, seven or next and no code holds their address,
    so `y >= 10` (bogus), `seven != 7` (init) and `next != 0` (afterarr) are
    decided by the image's bytes. `on` leaves bogus and init alone. live is
    stored to by set_live and esc has its address passed to take: written
    and taken keep their branch under `globals`.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">
c3
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="harness_stub"/>
</binaryimage>
